# Naked egg: a membrane water-transfer comparison
#
# The prepared naked_egg is explicitly an egg-white-composition surrogate
# behind a semipermeable membrane. It is not a simulated whole egg: shell
# removal is the separate chalk-and-vinegar route, and yolk, elasticity and
# final equilibrium size are outside this model.
register lv2

# In plain water the bath has fewer dissolved particles than the declared
# interior, so water moves into the coherent object.
add v1 water 150g
add v1 naked_egg 50g
wait 3600s
look v1

# Sugar raises the bath osmolarity. With the same object and clock, water now
# moves out. Ordinary decant/filter commands deliberately leave the coherent
# object behind; there is no invented whole-object pickup command.
new beaker
add v2 water 100g
add v2 sucrose 1mol
add v2 naked_egg 50g
wait 3600s
look v2
